From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:35:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/35] minimize: reload the config files on inotify instead of
 every 2 s

The ignore, detail and sizes files were stat'ed every 2 s, so an edit
showed up to 2 s late and the panel woke up for nothing. They are now
watched with the same inotify machinery as the tab files: the
~/.config/minimize-ws directory for writes, renames and deletes of the
three files, and ~/.config for the directory being created later. When
inotify is not available it still polls every 2 s by modification time.
An event re-reads the file even when its mtime did not change, so a
write within the timestamp granularity of the last read is not missed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BLrpLk9FRLLBEsz36L16sW

